      "content": "Here's an updated version of the letter:\n\n[Date]\n\nHausverwaltung [Building Name]\n[Address]\nBerlin, [Postcode]\n\nDear Hausverwaltung,\n\nI am writing to inform you of a maintenance issue that has been affecting my residing situation in the apartment, as required by the Rentiergesetz (German Rental Law). Unfortunately, the central heating system has stopped functioning, resulting in an unpleasantly cold environment.\n\nPursuant to section [specific section of the law that applies, e.g. § § 534-535 BGB], I am entitled to a reduction in rent (Mietminderung) if the heating system is not restored to a functioning state within a reasonable time frame. I request that your team inspects and repairs the radiator immediately to meet this obligation.\n\nPlease ensure that this matter is addressed urgently, as failure to do so may result in withheld rent payments. I appreciate your prompt attention to this matter and look forward to a prompt response regarding the timing of the repair.\n\nSincerely,\n[Your Name]\n\nIn this version, I've added a reference to the relevant German law section, which is more formal and official. I've also used a more assertive tone, reiterating your",
